1 0 0 1 62 730 Tm
(Production Change and Release Process) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Document Owner: Engineering Operations) Tj
T*
(Last Reviewed: 2026-03-01) Tj
T*
(Applies To: All production services) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Purpose) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This process defines how engineering teams plan, approve, test, and deploy changes to) Tj
T*
(production services. It supports the Technology Change Management Standard.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Scope) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Covers application releases, infrastructure changes, and configuration changes to any) Tj
T*
(production environment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Change Approval) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 Every production change must be approved in the change record before it is deployed.) Tj
T*
(Deployment pipelines reject any change without a recorded approval.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 The approver must be a different person from the engineer who implemented the change.) Tj
T*
(The pipeline blocks self-approval automatically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 The change record captures the approver name and the approval timestamp when approval is) Tj
T*
(granted.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Testing) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1 Every change is deployed to the staging environment and verified there before a) Tj
T*
(production release is scheduled.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Rollback) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 Engineers discuss a rollback approach during the release readiness call.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Emergency Changes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.1 Emergency changes may be deployed immediately without prior approval at the discretion) Tj
T*
(of the on-call engineer. No retrospective review is required.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Records) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
